{"id": "unknown-2026-09-27-002", "date": "2026-09-27", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 39, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India eases origin documentation for UK imports under CETA", "content": "CBIC has eased customs documentation for importers claiming preferential duties on UK-origin goods under the India-UK CETA. \nA valid Origin Declaration will generally suffice, with Form-I required only when customs identify specific origin risks. \nThe move reduces paperwork and compliance burdens, potentially speeding up clearance for eligible shipments.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-eases-origin-documentation-for-uk-imports-under-ceta-313796-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
